error[E0277]: this query states no row limit, so it cannot materialize rows
  --> tests/ui/query_unbounded_fetch_all.rs:14:24
   |
14 |     materialize_rows::<Unbounded>();
   |                        ^^^^^^^^^ needs a `.limit(n)` earlier in the chain
   |
   = help: the trait `BoundedRead` is not implemented for `boogy_sdk::query::Unbounded`
   = note: Without a limit the store answers with a page of its own choosing (BOOGY_STORE_MAX_PAGE_ROWS, default 1000 rows) and returns no cursor and no total, so a truncated answer is indistinguishable from a complete one.
   = note: If the set is bounded by construction — a top-N, an `is_in` over N ids, an existence probe — say so with `.limit(n)`.
   = note: If it grows with the tenant, use `.limit(n).cursor(token)` and end on `.fetch_page(|row| ..)`, which returns the token that continues the listing.
